@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="saps-content-header">
    <h1 class="h3 mb-0">About the SAPS Crime Pre-Reporting System</h1>
    <div class="saps-breadcrumb">Home / About</div>
</div>

<p class="text-muted mb-4">
    The SAPS Crime Pre-Reporting System lets a member of the public submit a preliminary record of a crime
    online, before it is opened as an official docket at a police station, and gives SAPS personnel the tools
    to review, process, escalate, and refer that record through to resolution.
</p>

<div class="card saps-card mb-4">
    <div class="saps-panel-header"><span><i class="bi bi-flag"></i> Our Mission</span></div>
    <div class="p-4">
        <p class="mb-0">
            Victims too often face improper refusal to open cases, are sent between stations, or are left with
            no proof they ever reported anything at all. This system exists to close that gap: the moment you
            submit a preliminary report, an early, timestamped digital record is created &mdash; giving you
            proof your report was heard, and giving SAPS a traceable record of every step that follows.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card saps-card mb-4">
    <div class="saps-panel-header"><span><i class="bi bi-diagram-3"></i> How It Works</span></div>
    <div class="p-4">
        <ol class="mb-0">
            <li class="mb-2"><strong>Submit a preliminary report.</strong> Describe the incident, date, and
                location, and share your device's location so it can be routed to the SAPS station nearest you.
                You get a reference number immediately as proof of submission.</li>
            <li class="mb-2"><strong>A SAPS Officer reviews it.</strong> Once accepted, it's opened as an
                official case docket with a CAS number.</li>
            <li class="mb-2"><strong>Track, refer, or escalate.</strong> Log in anytime to see your docket's
                status, message the officer handling it, or escalate directly to a Station Commander if it's
                unresolved. An officer can also refer a docket to another station or specialised unit.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card saps-card mb-4">
    <div class="saps-panel-header"><span><i class="bi bi-stars"></i> What Else the System Offers</span></div>
    <div class="p-4">
        <div class="row g-4">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="d-flex gap-3">
                    <i class="bi bi-file-earmark-check-fill text-primary fs-4"></i>
                    <div>
                        <strong>Affidavits</strong>
                        <div class="text-muted small">Complete a sworn statement online, confirm your identity
                            with a live photo and ID document, and have it electronically certified by an
                            officer at your nearest station &mdash; no walking in with a blank form required.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="d-flex gap-3">
                    <i class="bi bi-bell-fill text-primary fs-4"></i>
                    <div>
                        <strong>Notifications</strong>
                        <div class="text-muted small">Get notified in-app and by email whenever your report,
                            docket, or affidavit changes status.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="d-flex gap-3">
                    <i class="bi bi-clock-history text-primary fs-4"></i>
                    <div>
                        <strong>Full audit trail</strong>
                        <div class="text-muted small">Every view, update, and sensitive action is logged
                            against the user, time, and (where relevant) IP address responsible for it.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="d-flex gap-3">
                    <i class="bi bi-shield-lock-fill text-primary fs-4"></i>
                    <div>
                        <strong>Role-based access</strong>
                        <div class="text-muted small">Every account can only see and do what its role permits
                            &mdash; see "Roles in This System" below.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card saps-card mb-4">
    <div class="saps-panel-header"><span><i class="bi bi-people-fill"></i> Roles in This System</span></div>
    <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table mb-0 align-middle">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th style="width:220px;">Role</th>
                    <th>What they can do</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="badge text-bg-primary">Complainant</span></td>
                    <td>Submits preliminary reports and affidavits, tracks their own dockets, messages the
                        officer handling their case, and escalates unresolved matters. This is the role
                        anyone can self-register for.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="badge text-bg-success">SAPS Officer</span></td>
                    <td>Reviews preliminary reports and affidavits routed to their station, opens and updates
                        official dockets, and refers dockets to other stations or units.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="badge text-bg-warning">Station Commander</span></td>
                    <td>Oversees dockets and affidavits at their station and resolves escalations raised
                        against it.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="badge text-bg-secondary">System Administrator</span></td>
                    <td>Manages user accounts and stations, reviews the system-wide audit trail, and exports
                        reports &mdash; without routinely accessing case content to do so.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card saps-card mb-4">
    <div class="p-4 d-flex align-items-start gap-3">
        <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle-fill text-warning fs-3"></i>
        <div>
            <strong>Not an emergency service.</strong>
            <div class="text-muted">If anyone is in immediate danger, contact your local emergency services
                directly &mdash; don't wait for a submission here to be reviewed.</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card saps-card mb-4">
    <div class="saps-panel-header"><span><i class="bi bi-envelope"></i> Get in Touch</span></div>
    <div class="p-4 mb-0">
        <p class="mb-0">
            Questions about how the system works, or about a specific case, are best directed to the station
            handling it. For questions about the system itself or your account, see our
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Faq">FAQ</a>, or contact
            <a href="mailto:support@saps.local">support@saps.local</a>. For questions about your personal
            information, see our <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
